  "notes": "Cash-basis audit (modified cash). Governmental lines from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Fund Balances - Cash Basis, Governmental Funds (p4) TOTAL column (General, Special Revenue, Debt Service funds). Transfers in/out 19,942 (General to Debt Service) printed inside the revenue and expenditure totals. Roll-forward: 1,472,984 + 414,866 - 676,975 + 19,942 - 19,942 = 1,210,875. Beginning cash not printed (only fund balance); ending cash = 'Cash or cash equivalents' 824,443 (p3), certificates of deposit 380,294 as investments, cash at county treasurer 6,138 recorded on the balance sheet. Business-type: single Enterprise Fund (Sewer, Water, Trash) from p6, matching the Statement of Activities business columns (p2): 411,408 + 462,126 - 406,667 = 466,867. Balance sheet: governmental funds balance sheet (p3) totals equal the government-wide figures (1,210,875) so its lines and fund balance classifications are used; business lines from the proprietary statement of net position (p5). Component unit (Verdigre Library Foundation) excluded. Detail: General Fund and Special Fund budget schedules (pp7-8; zero-actual lines Federal receipts, Capital improvements, Other capital outlay skipped); no Debt Service Fund schedule (not added). Enterprise Fund detail from the proprietary statement (no budget schedule). The Statement of Activities general revenue labels do not match the fund statement labels for the same amounts (see decision_needed). Read pages 1-8 of 8"
